[{:db/id -1, :doc/id "doc-ayatori-bench-coscientist-iteration-24", :doc/title "ayatori Co-Scientist Iteration 24 — eleven of 29 operations with the reference on every parameter; 337 B live per quad", :doc/path "bench/coscientist-iteration-24.edn", :doc/body "# Co-Scientist iteration 24 - eleven of the 29 operations with the reference on every parameter, and the footprint number that changes M3\n\n> Seed: iteration 23's S13 - load the attributes the subset lacked so\n> IS1/IS3/IS6 have data, and measure the per-quad footprint for M3.\n> Judge: bench/benchmark.edn v2; rung SF1 subset (now with profiles,\n> friendship dates, forums); origin :cross-host, path :lan; impl :datalog.\n\n## Generate\n\n  Loaded: person gender/birthday/creationDate/locationIP/browserUsed and\n  city (6 x 9,892); the knows creationDate reified per direction\n  (kn:<a>:<b> with knows/person, knows/friend, knows/creationDate --\n  3 x 361,246, the same data-model cost `likes` already pays for an edge\n  property); the forum of every kept post with title, creationDate and\n  moderator (5,507 forums). 810,221 -> 2,004,832 quads.\n\n  IS1 (profile), IS3 (friends with friendship date, newest first, id asc\n  on ties), IS6 (forum of the root post with moderator) as Datalog and\n  index twins; gate widened to 1,082 parameters; Cypher for the three\n  added to the harness with the Neo4j loader carrying the new properties,\n  KNOWS creationDate, Forum nodes, CONTAINER_OF and HAS_MODERATOR.\n\n  Prediction: zero disagreements; the 11-op mix at 8 slots at or near the\n  8-op column (2941) since IS1/IS6 are point lookups; IS3 heavier (a\n  friends list is ~100 rows).\n\n## Rank\n\n  Reference (paired run on simeon, one JVM, both engines):\n    ic02 98/0  ic07 98/0  ic08 98/0  ic09 98/0\n    is1 98/0   is2 98/0   is3 98/0   is4 99/0   is5 99/0   is6 99/0   is7 99/0\n  Paired p50 ratio kotobase/Neo4j (highest-degree persons):\n    ic02 0.30  ic07 1.55  ic08 2.75  ic09 0.85\n\n  Footprint (gc twice, live heap before/after build, -Xmx12g):\n    2,004,832 quads -> 644 MB -> 337 B per quad\n\n  Served, LAN, 11-op mix:\n    slots  rate  on-time%  thru/s  rows  ic02 ic07 ic08 ic09  is1 is2 is3 is4 is5 is6 is7\n      8    2048  100.00   2047.5  49.6   3.8  2.4  2.1  6.6  2.2 3.5 6.7 2.1 2.1 2.1 2.0\n      8    2560   34.67   2225.5\n     32    4096  100.00   4088.9  49.6   7.1  5.8  5.5 11.2  5.6 7.3 11.9 5.6 5.5 5.4 5.4\n     32    4608   53.32   4242.6\n\n## Reflect\n\n  - Agreement held. Throughput did not: 2047 against the 8-op column's\n    2941 at 8 slots, 4089 against 5118 at 32. The price is IS3: a\n    friends list is ~100 rows with names and dates, so the mean answer\n    went from 8.3 rows to 49.6 and IS3 costs 6.7 ms served -- one\n    operation in eleven, mostly EDN printing and transfer. Under the\n    growth rule this is a TRADE, and the row says what was bought (three\n    operations, 11/29 with reference) and what it cost.\n  - The footprint corrects a number I had been carrying: 337 B live per\n    quad, not ~1.6 KB. The earlier figure was the SUT's USED heap with\n    garbage in it, read off /ldbc/meta. Full SF1 (~16-20M quads) is\n    ~6-7 GB live and fits simeon; SF3 too; SF30 still does not. M3's\n    first step is closer than iteration 21 said.\n  - The reified friendship date is 54% of all quads now. An edge\n    property costs three datoms per direction here; the LDBC mix asks\n    for it in exactly one operation.\n\n## Meta\n\nVerdict under bench/benchmark.edn v2: TRADE (mix 8 -> 11 of 29 at lower\nthroughput on the same slots; price named). M1 stands at 11/29 served\nwith reference, 0 with updates.\n\nSeeds for iteration 25, in order:\n\n  - S2 (rung, M3): full SF1 on simeon -- the footprint says it fits.\n    Load time is the first number (the 35k subset builds in 2 s; the\n    full reply forest and 2M comments are the loader's cost), then the\n    11-op mix on SF1 proper with the empty share at ~0.\n  - S14 (IS3 cost): the answer is the payload; measure EDN print/transfer\n    against a compact encoding, and whether the gate's row equality\n    survives it.\n  - S15 (IC coverage): IC01/IC03/IC04/IC05... need tags, places,\n    universities, companies -- static tables; each is more quads and one\n    more operation with reference.\n  - M2 (updates) stays the design step.\n"}]
